{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791134115,"nonce":"ejZT4RvA4kE5pDaUB2zWY6EjYuI=","title":"query(element): a shorthand over Interaction.of(node) to drive an element from code","message":"Today, controlling an element from code means reaching past the element to its node: `Interaction.of(el.node).onClick(...)`, `Interaction.of(el.node).setFocusable(true)`, plus `Identity.of(tree, el.node.id)` for attributes and classes, and `el.node.set(Prop.X, ...)` for layout. That is three entry points and a node id for what users think of as \"this element\". About 46 files in haxe/ and components/ call `Interaction.of(...)`.\n\nWanted: a `query(element)` macro that takes an element (and maybe a node, or an id or selector within a tree) and returns one handle with everything, so users write the shorthand:\n\n    query(button).onClick(_ -\u003e save()).focusable(true);\n    query(panel).onPointerDown(e -\u003e drag(e));\n    query(row).attr(\"data-state\", \"open\").addClass(\"selected\");\n\nThe handle exposes the binding functions `Interaction` gives (onClick, onPointerDown, onPointerUp, onPointerMove, onPointerEnter, onPointerLeave, onWheel, onKeyDown, onKeyUp, onTextInput, onComposition, onFocus, onBlur, setFocusable, setDisabled, focus) and programmatic control: attributes and classes through Identity, layout props through the node, bounds, focus, and maybe a dispatched click for tests and scripts.\n\nShape to decide:\n- a macro or an inline abstract over the node: an `abstract Query(Node)` with inline forwarding adds no allocation and needs no macro; a macro buys `query(\"#id\")` or `query(\".class\")` lookups resolved in a tree, and compile-time errors;\n- whether it returns `Interaction` itself extended, or a new type that forwards to Interaction, Identity and Node;\n- chaining: each call returns the handle;\n- whether components adopt it internally (replace `Interaction.of(x.node)` across components/) or it stays a user-facing shorthand first.\n\nHaxe-first, typed: no Dynamic, and nothing a plain Haxe user cannot discover through completion.","files":null}]}